-- title:
--   From HTo G Bool Type Filtered Outcome Sum
-- statement:
--   **Partitioning by failure status and tuple type does not change the outcome sum.**
--
--   Let $n\in\mathbb{N}$, let $\mathcal O$ and $\mathcal O_n$ be the finite completed-outcome sets, and let $\tau(gs)\in\{0,1\}^n$. For a Boolean status $b(g)\in\{0,1\}$ and any $F$,
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{b\in\{0,1\}}\sum_{\tau\in\{0,1\}^n}\sum_{\substack{g\in\mathcal O,\ b(g)=b,\ gs\in\mathcal O_n,\ \tau(gs)=\tau}}F(b,\tau,g,gs)=\sum_{g\in\mathcal O}\sum_{gs\in\mathcal O_n}F\left(b(g),\tau(gs),g,gs\right).
--   $$
--
--   The unrestricted sum assigns each outcome and tuple to its unique Boolean and type fibers. This reindexing is used in the pointwise adjacent-stage identities and in the self-consistency context estimate.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
